Z||000037||AkursedX||04-15-2001||03:35 PM||||Not that I'm a fan of Sony Xplod, but it looks great in that car!  Matches and compliments the interior perfectly!  That is one awesome setup!!  ||||reg||1
Z||000038||AusFiero||04-16-2001||08:00 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by AkursedX:<BR><B>Not that I'm a fan of Sony Xplod, but it looks great in that car!  Matches and compliments the interior perfectly!  That is one awesome setup!!  </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Ahhhh someone who has seen my reason for going the Explode system. Personally I am a Pioneer fan, but as I told my wife when I bought the Sony, "I shopped like a woman cause it looked pretty in the car"  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <P>Also with a sub 7" or 8" from your ear it has the desired effect. Although I have already decided I need 2 6X9 speakers behind the seats to add a better mid range "bass wise" to the current combination, or a better cd player. Has plenty of top and bottom end but is missing that little extra in the mid range area.<P>Will answer lots of the other questions above as I go through them.<P>For some outside pics of my car at the recent Australian Pontiac Nationals that I just returned from today go to  <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/006899.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/006899.html</A> ||||reg||14
Z||000039||AusFiero||04-16-2001||09:04 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by 85Josh:<BR><B>I love the aluminum switches! Are they a custom job, or is it paint?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>They are painted. If you intend to try it take time with the preparation of the plastic switches and vents. I found a wipe over with a damp thinners rag not long before painting softened the surface of the old plastic and made the acrylic paint really bite into it. Paint colour is an Australian GM colour so I am sure you will have a similar one there.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000040||85Josh||04-16-2001||10:23 PM||||Cool. I'll have to try it out on some of my spare parts. Thanks, your interior is quite an inspiration.<P>WOOHOO! first post on the second page! (yeah, I got no life.)<BR>------------------<BR>85 2M4(Lil' Bit)<p>[This message has been edited by 85Josh (edited 04-16-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000041||Black88GT||04-17-2001||01:20 AM||||Oh yeah please keep us updated on those door pods, its exactly what I have been looking for!<P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD - MAFOA<BR>         <IMG SRC="http://88database.homestead.com/files/AF.gif">    <BR><I>"Once you go black, you never go back..."</I><BR><I>"The Customer Can Have Any Color He Wants So Long As It's Black" </I> -Henry Ford||||reg||14
Z||000042||AusFiero||04-21-2001||04:35 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Black88GT:<BR><B>Oh yeah please keep us updated on those door pods, its exactly what I have been looking for!<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Will take some pictures of the pods tomorrow and post them as their own topic. <P>On other replies. dash is a reskinned fibreglass version. So it pretty much is a complete dopleganger. All the rest of the bits are relatively easy to move. Indicator switch is a little annoying on the left but we get plenty of imports that way RHD from the factory so it isn't so bad.<P>Aussie gear box shift pattern is the same the USA one. 1st gear is up and left in our case. I can't imagine shifting with my right hand by the way. Thats usually reserved for when you a passenger and the driver is trying to drive while taking a mobile phone call and eat a big mac all at once.<P>The console plans for the sub I am still drawing, will get to them as I get time.<P>||||reg||1
